-- ============================================================================
-- H5 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Quantitative Risk Assessment, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/qra/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: HOW OFTEN, AND WHAT IS ONE PERSON'S INDIVIDUAL RISK. An
-- event tree's leaf frequency is the initiating frequency times the branch
-- probabilities on its path, and every branch set sums to one within a
-- tolerance; delayed ignition is conditional on no immediate ignition; the
-- direct ignition table and the flash fire and explosion split are taught and
-- always stated in a capstone; location-specific individual risk is the sum of
-- frequency times a STATED probability of death; individual risk per annum
-- spreads it over the year one person spends at each place. Digest sections 1
-- to 14, and section 34.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A tree that closes is valid arithmetic
-- whatever it means. The Associate capstone grades two outcome frequencies,
-- two LSIRs and two IRPAs, and grades no PLL, FAR, F-N figure, ALARP band or
-- cost-benefit figure.
-- ============================================================================

values ('qra', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-qra-answers","title":"What a Quantitative Risk Assessment Answers","lesson_keys":["l01-what-a-qra-answers","l02-frequencies-per-year-and-probabilities","l03-where-the-probability-of-death-comes-from","l04-the-refusals-by-name"]},{"key":"m02-event-trees","title":"Event Trees","lesson_keys":["l01-a-tree-of-branches","l02-every-branch-set-sums-to-one","l03-the-leaf-frequency","l04-pooling-leaves-into-outcomes","l05-a-tree-that-does-not-close"]},{"key":"m03-a-flammable-release","title":"A Flammable Release","lesson_keys":["l01-immediate-and-delayed-ignition","l02-delayed-ignition-is-conditional","l03-flash-fire-and-explosion","l04-the-direct-ignition-table","l05-forgetting-a-branch"]},{"key":"m04-location-specific-individual-risk","title":"Location-Specific Individual Risk","lesson_keys":["l01-risk-at-a-place","l02-summing-the-contributions","l03-outdoors-unprotected-all-the-time","l04-a-published-contribution-reproduced"]},{"key":"m05-individual-risk-per-annum","title":"Individual Risk per Annum","lesson_keys":["l01-one-person-many-places","l02-hours-and-fractions-of-the-year","l03-one-place-at-a-time","l04-the-vulnerability-factor"]},{"key":"m06-one-person-end-to-end","title":"One Person, End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-risk-along-a-transect","l02-contours-on-a-plot-plan","l03-what-individual-risk-does-not-say","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
